docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","content":"Fluid exposes a Kubernetes `Dataset` to application pods. Curvine can be used as the cache runtime behind that Dataset, or as an existing storage cluster that Fluid only mounts.","locale":"en"},"28":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-26","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","content":"For new Fluid deployments, start with **CacheRuntime**. It lets Fluid create Curvine master, worker, and FUSE client pods, and it is the path that supports CacheRuntime data operations such as `DataLoad`.","locale":"en"},"29":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-27","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#choose-an-integration-mode","content":"| Mode         | Use it when                                                     | What Fluid starts                             | Main resources                                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| CacheRuntime | You want Fluid to manage a Curvine cache cluster in Kubernetes. | Curvine master, worker, and client/FUSE pods. | `CacheRuntimeClass`, `Dataset`, `CacheRuntime` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"30":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-28","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#choose-an-integration-mode","content":"| Mode        | Use it when                                                                        | What Fluid starts          | Main resources                                 |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n|