-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#3-install-the-csi-driver","content":"Create a StorageClass that points at the master. Each PVC gets its own directory under `fs-path` in Curvine:","locale":"en"},"1892":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-32","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#4-mount-a-volume-in-a-pod","content":"Save a PVC and a test pod that mounts it at `/data`:","locale":"en"},"1893":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-33","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#4-mount-a-volume-in-a-pod","content":"Apply it and wait for the pod. The pod becomes Ready only after the PVC is bound and the volume is mounted:","locale":"en"},"1894":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-34","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#4-mount-a-volume-in-a-pod","content":"Write a file and read it back:","locale":"en"},"1895":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-35","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#4-mount-a-volume-in-a-pod","content":"`/data` is a Curvine FUSE mount:","locale":"en"},"1896":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-36","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#4-mount-a-volume-in-a-pod","content":"The file is stored in Curvine, not in the pod. List it with the `cv` CLI in the master container:","locale":"en"},"1897":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-37","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#4-mount-a-volume-in-a-pod","content":"To confirm the data outlives the pod, recreate the pod and read the file again:","locale":"en"},"1898":{"id":"/d