 source path.","locale":"en"},"3337":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-120","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#jobs---load-and-export-jobs","content":"The Jobs page shows manual `cv load` / `cv export` jobs with their per-task\nprogress. With the standalone Transfer service enabled, live Transfer jobs move to\nthe Transfers page; Jobs keeps the legacy Master-side view and `fs_mode`\nauto-export diagnostics.","locale":"en"},"3338":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-121","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#observability-and-operations","content":"`/observability` renders charts from the built-in collector, or from Prometheus\nwhen `[web.observability].mode` is `prometheus` or `auto`. `/operations` is the\nhealth view on top of that data: open alerts, which provider is active, and how\nmuch of the scrape target set is actually reporting. When FUSE scraping is off\n(`[web.observability.fuse].enabled = false`), the coverage panel correctly reports\nFUSE targets as missing.","locale":"en"},"3339":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-122","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#observability-and-operations","content":"Through the web management interface, Curvine provides users with comprehensive cluster management and monitoring capabilities, greatly simplifying the operational work of distributed cache systems and improving management efficiency and system observability.","locale":"en"},"3340":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","type":"page","content":"Best Practices","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","locale":"en"},"3341":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/best-practi