[5416,"CSI 节点插件通过 FUSE 挂载卷，因此 kind 节点上需要有 `/dev/fuse`。kind 节点以特权容器运行，可以看到宿主机的设备，无需额外挂载。确认设备存在："],[6030,"CSI 驱动"],[364,"Current position (`pos`), device size, block size"],[860,"Cursor discovers the same skills without a slash command. If you are ever unsure what a skill does, open its `SKILL.md` — that file is the contract."],[4388,"Cursor 会自动发现这些 skill，不需要斜杠命令。如果你不确定某个 skill 具体做什么，打开它的 `SKILL.md` 看看——那份文件就是它的约定。"],[2035,"Curvine (QPS)"],[5570,"Curvine (QPS)"],[1951,"Curvine adopts a layered distributed architecture design that ensures clear component responsibilities with excellent scalability and high availability. The entire architecture is primarily divided into three layers: **control layer** (Master), **storage layer** (Workers), and **access layer** (clients: FUSE, SDK, CLI), which collaborate to complete data storage, processing, and management tasks."],[2118,"Curvine adopts a modular codebase. The main components in the current `main` branch are:"],[2002,"Curvine adopts distributed architecture design with multi-replica mechanisms and failover mechanisms to ensure system high availability:"],[3057,"Curvine also exposes a FUSE file system interface. After mounting it, for example via `bin/curvine-fuse.sh start`, you can operate on the mount point with normal Linux tools:"],[1,"Curvine and Fluid Integration"],[946,"Curvine commonly uses these inputs together:"],[1360,"Curvine config (`config.*`)"],[3500,"Curvine configuration adjustment example:"],[1952,"Curvine consists of three main server-side roles plus clients and UFS:"],[2399,"Curvine CSI has three moving parts:"],[5936,"Curvine CSI 主要由三部分组成："],[155,"Curvine design doc"],[3684,"Curvine design doc"],[3529,"Curvine Documentation"],[2717,"Curvine does not follow Close-to-Open. Instead, it is fully consistent with local disk file semantics:"],[2015,"Curvine exposes multiple access paths for analytics, AI, and data infrastructure workloads, including the Rust CLI, FUSE, and Java/Python SDK bindings."],[2636,"Curvine follows local disk usage habits."],[3521,"Curvine FUSE currently does not support page cache."],[3518,"Curvine FUSE currently supports FUSE2 and FUSE3. FUSE2's performance is approximately only 50% of FUSE3, so it's recommended to use FUSE3 in production environments."],[3419,"Curvine FUSE is fully asynchronous — `attr_timeout` and `entry_timeout` are optional. Increase them for read-heavy workloads with stable metadata:"],[6953,"Curvine FUSE is fully asynchronous — `attr_timeout` and `entry_timeout` are optional. Increase them for read-heavy workloads with stable metadata:"],[2163,"Curvine FUSE supports:"],[1726,"curvine fuse Use Cases"],[5262,"curvine fuse 使用场景"],[5698,"Curvine FUSE 支持："],[7055,"curvine fuse目前不支持page cache。"],[7052,"curvine fuse目前支持fuse2、fuse3；fuse2的性能大约只有fuse3的50%，因此建议在生产环境中使用fuse3。"],[1569,"Curvine has no minimum resource requirements and can support extremely high concurrency and traffic with very small resources. Here is a reference configuration:"],[271,"Curvine integrates with OpenDAL (Open Data Access Layer) at its core, providing powerful storage ecosystem support. This integration enables Curvine to work seamlessly with various storage backends while maintaining a unified interface."],[345,"Curvine interacts with the SPDK C library through a thin FFI layer that insulates Rust code from SPDK's C ABI. Three techniques are used:"],[171,"Curvine is a distributed file cache layer. The **Master** manages metadata and block placement; **Workers** store block data and serve read/write; **Clients** (FUSE, SDK, CLI) talk to Master for metadata and to Workers for data. Metadata is replicated via **Raft** for high availability."],[2629,"Curvine is a distributed file cache system. It integrates storage media inside the cluster and remote storage resources to build a unified file directory space, and provides a directly mountable filesystem to external users."],[2013,"Curvine is a high-performance distributed cache system written in Rust and released under the Apache 2.0 license. It provides a unified cached file-system view over external storage systems, with low-latency metadata access, high-throughput data access, and POSIX-compatible FUSE integration."],[2025,"Curvine is designed for high-performance, high-concurrency, and massive data caching scenarios:"],[2638,"Curvine is not limited to sequential or append-only writes. It supports writing at any file position at any time, which fits scenarios such as databases and large-file modification that require random reads and writes."],[5261,"curvine master、curvine worker 与 curvine fuse 的关系"],[208,"Curvine Metadata Architecture"],[2061,"Curvine Open Source Edition (GiB/s)"],[2089,"Curvine Open Source Edition (GiB/s)"],[5596,"Curvine Open Source Edition (GiB/s)"],[5624,"Curvine Open Source Edition (GiB/s)"],[2743,"Curvine optimization: Curvine tracks opened files. If a file is modified, the page cache automatically becomes invalid to ensure the latest data is read."],[2008,"Curvine Overview"],[2770,"Curvine path, or CV path: the unified logical path inside the cluster. It always starts with `/` and belongs to Curvine's `cv://` namespace. On the client side, it is the mount point directory that users can directly access."],[2772,"Curvine persists the mount table in metadata, so there is no need to remount when Curvine restarts. However, some rules must be followed:"],[2767,"Curvine provides a UFS (Unified File System) view to manage all supported distributed storage systems, including local filesystems, S3/MinIO, HDFS, and others. In simple terms, Curvine UFS mounting creates a path mapping that integrates external storage systems into Curvine's own filesystem. Users no longer need to remember different storage access methods and can access all storage through one unified interface."],[3247,"Curvine provides an intuitive and user-friendly web management interface that allows users to monitor cluster status in real-time, browse the file system, inspect worker nodes, follow load and transfer jobs, and read the effective configuration — all from a browser. The web interface serves as a visual operations platform for cluster operations and daily management, so most inspection tasks no longer require the CLI."],[1528,"Curvine provides compilation images on Docker Hub: `curvine/curvine-compile:latest` (and optionally `curvine/curvine-compile:build-cached` with cached dependencies)."],[2310,"Curvine provides multi-language SDKs so applications can access the Curvine filesystem via RPC (metadata from Master, block data from Workers) without using FUSE."],[70,"Curvine reports values that the master can return cheaply: cached bytes, cache capacity, and file count. `ufsTotal`, `cachedPercentage`, and `cacheHitRatio` stay `0` until Curvine has authoritative UFS total and hit-ratio metadata. This avoids showing a cache-capacity percentage as a Dataset cache percentage."],[813,"Curvine Roadmap"],[5754,"Curvine S3 网关通过 S3 兼容的 HTTP API 暴露 Curvine 集群。已经支持 S3 协议的工具——AWS CLI、MinIO Client、boto3 或任意 S3 SDK——无需 FUSE 或 Curvine 原生客户端即可读写 Curvine 路径。网关使用 AWS Signature V2/V4 对每个请求进行认证，并将 bucket 和 key 映射为 Curvine 文件系统操作。"],[546,"Curvine Small File Read Performance Test"],[2640,"Curvine supports advanced POSIX features to meet complex business requirements."],[243,"Curvine supports fs-mode. Its core function is to synchronize metadata and file data to the underlying unified file system, UFS, forming a dual guarantee of local storage plus disk fallback. This avoids data loss without affecting system performance:"],[2720,"Curvine supports multiple clients concurrently reading and writing the same file, but it has clear characteristics:"],[1544,"Curvine supports multiple storage backends including OSS, HDFS, S3, MinIO, and more. By default, these are integrated via OpenDAL. Curvine also provides optimized implementations for OSS and HDFS. Select backends with `--ufs` when building:"],[2649,"Curvine supports multiple storage media tiers. With simple configuration, users can specify data storage priority to balance speed and cost."],[82,"Curvine then runs:"],[2014,"Curvine uses a classic Master/Worker architecture. Master nodes manage metadata and cluster coordination, while Worker nodes store and serve data blocks. Metadata consistency and high availability are provided through Raft."],[331,"Curvine uses SPDK as a **remote block device** — the NVMe-oF target can be a physical NVMe drive on the same host, a dedicated SPDK target container, or a remote storage node. The Worker opens `SpdkBdev` handles (analogous to `LocalFile`) and issues read/write I/O through the `BlockIO` trait."],[1852,"Curvine uses TOML-formatted configuration files. An example configuration is located at `conf/curvine-cluster.toml`. The main configuration items include:"],[732,"Curvine version or commit"],[2498,"Curvine volume parameters"],[6254,"Curvine 不遵循 Close-to-Open，而是和本地磁盘文件语义完全一致："],[3530,"Curvine 与 Fluid 集成"],[5561,"Curvine 为高性能、高并发以及海量数据缓存设计，可以在很多场景中使用："],[4281,"Curvine 仓库同时包含 Cargo workspace，以及若干用于打包、部署和测试的顶层目录。"],[6280,"Curvine 优化：会跟踪已打开文件，文件被修改则页缓存自动失效，保证读到最新数据"],[5388,"Curvine 使用 TOML 格式的配置文件。示例配置位于 `conf/curvine-cluster.toml`，主要配置项包括："],[3746,"Curvine 元数据架构的核心设计目标的明确且聚焦，主要围绕四大核心需求展开：一是支持千万至百亿级文件/目录的元数据存储，适配海量小文件、大文件混合的存储场景；二是保障高并发读写场景下的低延迟，应对频繁的文件创建、删除、修改等高频操作；三是实现分布式集群多节点数据一致，避免出现“本地修改后其他节点不可见”的问题；四是兼顾运维便捷性与成本可控，降低部署、监控和故障恢复的复杂度。"],[3777,"Curvine 元数据架构的核心逻辑，可概括为“三层分工、一个权衡、一个兜底”，既保证了速度和海量存储，又兼顾了数据一致性和运维便捷性："],[3737,"Curvine 元数据架构说明"],[6035,"Curvine 卷参数"],[3599,"Curvine 只上报 master 能低成本返回的值：已缓存字节数、缓存容量和文件数。`ufsTotal`、`cachedPercentage`、`cacheHitRatio` 暂时保持为 `0`，直到 Curvine 有权威的 UFS 总量和命中率元数据。这样可以避免把“缓存容量使用率”误写成“Dataset 缓存百分比”。"],[6696,"Curvine 团队评估后，要么将版本加入 `blocked_versions`，要么在本页记录该不兼容。"],[5378,"curvine 在 dockerhub 上提供了 `curvine/curvine-compile` 镜像"],[3800,"Curvine 在核心层面集成了 OpenDAL（Open Data Access Layer，开放数据访问层），为 Curvine 提供强大的存储生态支持。这种集成使得 Curvine 能够与各种存储后端无缝协作，同时保持统一的接口。"],[6173,"Curvine 完全贴合本地磁盘使用习惯。"],[6177,"Curvine 完整支持各